TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"attempt":1,"blocked":true,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/41","kind":"diagnosis","posted":true,"proposal":{"acceptanceCriteria":[{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n scripts/run-smoke.sh && grep -q '_supports_quant_scheme' scripts/run-smoke.sh && ! grep -Eq '(ok|admitted)[[:space:]]*,[[:space:]]*why[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*TritonExperts\\._supports_quant_scheme' scripts/run-smoke.sh"],"description":"The smoke script no longer unpacks the boolean _supports_quant_scheme hook into a two-tuple, still calls the hook, and remains syntax-clean.","id":"smoke-admission-contract"},{"argv":["bash","scripts/run-smoke.sh"],"description":"The in-container smoke runs to completion and exits 0 against the cp-build image.","id":"smoke-runs-green"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -c \"import json,os,sys; r=json.load(open('results/receipts/smoke.json')); assert r['status']=='pass', r['status']; assert r['data']['admission']['fp8_block_moe_admitted'] is True, r['data']['admission']; assert not os.path.exists('results/receipts/failed/smoke.json'), 'fail receipt shadows the pass'\""],"description":"A passing receipt exists at results/receipts/smoke.json, records fp8_block_moe_admitted true, and no fail receipt shadows it.","id":"smoke-receipt-pass"},{"argv":["bash","-euc","bash scripts/run-smoke.sh >/dev/null && git diff --quiet -- . && git diff --quiet --cached -- . && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no)\""],"description":"Re-running the smoke over an already-correct base leaves every tracked file byte-identical, per checkpoint purity.","id":"smoke-idempotent-on-tracked-paths"}],"dependencies":["cp-build"],"goal":"Grant a short implementation lane authority over scripts/run-smoke.sh and correct the admission probe so the in-container smoke grades the engine instead of tripping over its own call contract. Required changes: (1) In the admission() probe, stop unpacking the return of TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme as a two-tuple. The fork's hook (patches/0008) is a plain boolean predicate, as its own pinned tests assert. Call it as `admitted = bool(TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym))` when the attribute exists, and keep the existing missing-hook fallback reporting fp8_block_moe_admitted=false with reason 'no hook'. Preserve the receipt's data.admission shape ({\"fp8_block_moe_admitted\": bool, \"reason\": str}) so downstream receipt graders keep working; supply a reason string derived locally (for example 'bool predicate admitted' / 'bool predicate refused') rather than a value returned by the hook. Do not weaken the probe into a pass-by-default: a false predicate must still set status=fail and route the receipt to results/receipts/failed/. (2) Satisfy OVERSEER STANDING NOTE 2 (checkpoint purity) for results/receipts/smoke.json: the receipt's ts must not be a fresh strftime on every run. Before writing, read any existing committed results/receipts/smoke.json; if every measured fact in data is byte-identical to the new measurement, reuse the existing ts and rewrite the file byte-identically (or skip the write) so a re-run over an already-correct base leaves tracked files unchanged and exits 0. Only stamp a new timestamp when a measured fact actually changed. (3) Land the resulting passing receipt at results/receipts/smoke.json in the lane commit, and leave the trailing verifier's failed/-beats-passing precedence logic intact. Do not touch patches/, container/, or any engine source: the engine behaviour is already correct and was observed admitting block-FP8 fused MoE on gfx1151 during reproduction.","kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},"redacted":false,"retry":null,"taskId":"cp-smoke","verdict":"blocked"}
